  "findings": [
    "Current-blob CAS fences only the LATEST blob. When authority changes without changing LATEST, CAS-drop and CAS+intent can still select stale old-authority state.",
    "CAS+merge-intent preserves the loser but can lose the already-winning checkpoint if a new-authority writer overwrites it before the loser records an intent that references it.",
    "CAS+merge-intent without an applied merge identity can duplicate a compatible contribution after ambiguous merge response plus retry.",
    "Append-only per-checkpoint branch indexing before mutable selection, plus current-authority fencing and deterministic idempotent selection, had zero semantic loss, zero duplicate integration, and zero stale selection in this finite model.",
    "Authority-fenced fail-closed CAS had zero stale selection and zero duplicate integration, but can still lose discoverability of an applied winner after response loss + crash + later overwrite if no independent branch index/reference exists."
  ],
